format - make a new filesystem on a volume

  format hd0p3
  format -t fat16 sd1

Writes an empty FAT filesystem over the volume. Everything on it becomes
unreachable: the tables and the root directory are written afresh and
nothing reads the data area again.

The width is chosen from the volume's size unless `-t` names one. A
volume too small for the width asked for is refused.

Refused while the volume is mounted. Asks for the volume's name to be
typed before writing.
